class:: PipeWireLink
summary:: A connection between two ports on the PipeWire graph
categories:: External Control>PipeWire
related:: Classes/PipeWire, Classes/PipeWirePatch, Classes/PipeWirePort

description::

A value object describing one link (an output port connected to an input port),
as returned by link::Classes/PipeWire#*links:: and
link::Classes/PipeWirePatch#-links::. Remove it with
link::Classes/PipeWire#*disconnectLink:: using its link::#-id::.

ClassMethods::

method:: new
argument:: id
argument:: output
argument:: input
returns:: a PipeWireLink.

InstanceMethods::

method:: id
The PipeWire link id (an link::Classes/Integer::), stable for the life of the link.

method:: output
The full code::"node:port":: name of the output (source) port.

method:: input
The full code::"node:port":: name of the input (destination) port.

Examples::

code::
PipeWire.links.do { |lk|
    "% -> %  [id %]".format(lk.output, lk.input, lk.id).postln;
};

// remove the first link:
PipeWire.links.first !? { |lk| PipeWire.disconnectLink(lk.id) };
::
